          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-(x^2+6x+8)\\\\y&=-(x+2)(x+4)\\\\0&=-(x+2)(x+4)\\\\x&=-4\\text{ or }-2\\\\x_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=\\frac{-4-2}{2}=-3\\\\y_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=-(-3+2)(-3+4)=1\\\\y(0)&=-(0+2)(0+4)=-8\\end{align*}$$\nPlot $(-4,0)$, $(-2,0)$, $(0,-8)$ and $(-3,1)$. Draw a downward-opening parabola symmetric about $x=-3$.",
