        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x+1)(x+2)$. $x$-intercepts: $(-2,0)$ and $(-1,0)$; $y$-intercept: $(0,2)$. Turning point: $\\left(-\\frac32,-\\frac14\\right)$; opens upwards.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x+1)(x+2)\\\\0&=(x+1)(x+2)\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }-1\\\\x_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=\\frac{-2-1}{2}=-\\frac32\\\\y_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=\\left(-\\frac32+1\\right)\\left(-\\frac32+2\\right)=-\\frac14\\\\y(0)&=(0+1)(0+2)=2\\end{align*}$$\nPlot $(-2,0)$, $(-1,0)$, $(0,2)$ and $\\left(-\\frac32,-\\frac14\\right)$. Draw an upward-opening parabola symmetric about $x=-\\frac32$.",
