        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=4\\left(x+\\frac12\\right)\\left(x-\\frac32\\right)$. $x$-intercepts: $\\left(-\\frac12,0\\right)$ and $\\left(\\frac32,0\\right)$; $y$-intercept: $(0,-3)$. Turning point: $\\left(\\frac12,-4\\right)$; opens upwards.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(2x+1)(2x-3)\\\\y&=4\\left(x+\\frac12\\right)\\left(x-\\frac32\\right)\\\\0&=(2x+1)(2x-3)\\\\x&=-\\frac12\\text{ or }\\frac32\\\\x_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=\\frac{-\\frac12+\\frac32}{2}=\\frac12\\\\y_{\\mathrm{TP}}&=4\\left(\\frac12+\\frac12\\right)\\left(\\frac12-\\frac32\\right)=-4\\\\y(0)&=4\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\left(-\\frac32\\right)=-3\\end{align*}$$\nPlot $\\left(-\\frac12,0\\right)$, $\\left(\\frac32,0\\right)$, $(0,-3)$ and $\\left(\\frac12,-4\\right)$. Draw an upward-opening parabola symmetric about $x=\\frac12$.",
